course: dictionary
lesson: 12866
title: Enlisting: joining up or asking for help
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Enlisting has two meanings, and the words around it show you which one you need. «In 1914, many young men were enlisting in the army.» The army tells you that enlisting means joining up to serve in it.
explain: «Mia is enlisting her friends to clean up the beach.» Nobody is joining an army here. Mia is asking her friends for help, so enlisting means getting others to join in. Always ask: which meaning fits the clues?
explain: Look for the phrase around the word. «Enlisting the help of» means asking for and getting someone's help. «Enlisting volunteers» means signing up people who choose to help. Learn the phrase, and the word becomes clear.
fact: Enlisting means joining the army, navy or air force, or signing someone up for them.
fact: Enlisting someone's help means asking for and getting their help or support.
fact: «Enlisting» is the -ing form of the verb enlist. Enlist, enlists and enlisted are related words.
fact: At the start of the First World War in 1914, many young men were enlisting, and some lied about their age to do so.
fact: A volunteer is someone who chooses to help or work without being forced to.
exercise: «At the start of the First World War, many young men were enlisting.» What does enlisting mean here? | Writing letters home | Cooking a big dinner | Going on holiday | *Joining the army
exercise: «Sam is enlisting his brother to help wash the car.» What does enlisting mean here? | Hiding the car keys | *Getting his brother to help | Washing the dog | Selling the car
exercise: Which phrase means asking for and getting someone's help? | enlisting in the army | enlisting in the air force | enlisting in the navy | *enlisting the help of
test: Ben says, «Enlisting the help of Gran, we baked a cake.» What does enlisting the help of mean? | Feeding Gran the cake | *Asking Gran for her help and getting it | Making Gran sign a form | Ignoring Gran completely
test: Which sentence uses enlisting to mean joining up for the armed forces? | «The shop is enlisting new stock.» | *«She is enlisting in the air force next month.» | «He is enlisting a new bike.» | «We are enlisting our friends to clean the park.»
exam: «The school is enlisting volunteers to read with the younger children.» What does enlisting volunteers mean? | *Signing up people who choose to help | Hiding from the volunteers | Teaching the volunteers to cook | Sending the volunteers home
